WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:06.420
Many times when people think about somebody
becoming an entrepreneur they think about,

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.790
day one they had a job, day two they quit
their job, day three they started a business.

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:11.740
It just happens in three days.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.089
But it doesn't happen that way.

00:00:13.089 --> 00:00:20.369
Most people started their business being part-time
or they had a transitional phase into going

00:00:20.369 --> 00:00:21.369
full time.

00:00:21.369 --> 00:00:22.609
This isn't everybody, but this is a lot of
people.

00:00:22.609 --> 00:00:28.019
I think about when I interviewed Steve Wozniak,
co-founder of Apple, when he and Steve Jobs

00:00:28.019 --> 00:00:29.050
started the company together.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.320
I asked him a question, "So how was it when
you got started?"

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.870
He said, "I had a job, we were both working,
whether it was Atari or Toshiba, we had a

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:36.870
job.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:40.800
And then six months later when I noticed that
people wanted to buy the product, of Macintosh

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:46.289
and our computers, then I quit my job and
I went full time because I had benefits, etc.

00:00:46.289 --> 00:00:47.289
And then we started Apple.

00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:51.769
So there is that idea to know that a lot of
people start part-time.

00:00:51.769 --> 00:00:53.920
The key is to know when to go full time.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:01:00.440
So today I want to talk to you about 7 items
to think about when going full-time as an

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.539
entrepreneur Some of these have to do with
each other.

00:01:03.539 --> 00:01:05.510
Some of them are completely separate.

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:06.930
But it's 7 things to be thinking about.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:10.410
When someone calls or asks me the question,
"You know, Pat, I'm afraid, should I go.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:11.410
. . am I ready?

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:12.410
When am I fully ready?

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:13.410
Should I quit my job?

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.410
Should I go full time?

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:15.410
Should I do this?"

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:18.180
By the time I'm done with this video, the
people that are thinking about, "Am I ready

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:22.970
to go full time, and if yes, what date should
I put for me to go full time and become a

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:24.090
full-time entrepreneur?"

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.710
So let me get right into it.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:34.190
To me, I remember when I went full time, the
first thing I had to know that whatever product

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:40.530
you are selling as an entrepreneur, you have
a track record of selling that product.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:46.910
For example, if someone wants to become a
real estate agent, hypothetically, if you

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:51.830
never sold a single real-estate property,
and you go full-time the next day, and you

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:56.140
have nothing in place, nothing in savings,
nothing, you're just going to go full time

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:59.010
the next day, but you never sold, and you're
thinking your family and everyone is going

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:01.360
to buy from you, it's a bad idea.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.110
Now does it work every once in awhile?

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:06.640
Yes, but it's not the best idea for someone
to go full time right off the bat.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:12.459
I was selling investment products and insurance,
401ks, IRAs was what I was selling, and I

00:02:12.459 --> 00:02:15.090
had to know, "Patrick, do you know how to
sell these products?"

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:21.069
The moment I knew how to sell that product,
and the number I like is 50 sales, but 50

00:02:21.069 --> 00:02:25.769
sales is not in every business, and in real
estate, 50 sales, maybe you've sold six different

00:02:25.769 --> 00:02:26.769
homes.

00:02:26.769 --> 00:02:27.910
Or you've sold ten different homes.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.629
Then you may be ready to do that.

00:02:29.629 --> 00:02:33.439
If you've sold six homes, depending on the
type of market you're in, and sales you're

00:02:33.439 --> 00:02:37.219
in, it could be a $60,000 payday, it could
be a $100,000 payday.

00:02:37.219 --> 00:02:42.239
If you're in the Arkansas market, with $60,000
homes, it may be a $15,000 payday.

00:02:42.239 --> 00:02:43.739
So it's all relative on where you are.

00:02:43.739 --> 00:02:46.930
But I want to be able to know that I have
a track record of selling that product and

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:51.620
making money selling that product and not
a one-off success story or two.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:56.239
Multiple success stories depending on the
industry you're part of.

00:02:56.239 --> 00:02:59.819
The next thing on when you're ready to go
full time is this.

00:02:59.819 --> 00:03:03.629
Say I have a job and I'm making eight grand
a month, hypothetically.

00:03:03.629 --> 00:03:07.889
And I want to go full time in my business,
and my business is only paying me $1100 a

00:03:07.889 --> 00:03:10.180
month, the last three months I made $1100.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:15.140
And by the way, never go full time on one
big month.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:20.799
The way I gauge my income is I take my six-month
income, and whatever it is I make in my business

00:03:20.799 --> 00:03:26.280
every month, and I take the lowest number
of the six months, and that's my real income,

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:27.280
hypothetically.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:32.659
If month one I made six grand, month two I
made $1500.

00:03:32.659 --> 00:03:39.040
Month three I made three, month four I made
$1100, month five I made $700, and month six

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:43.300
I made $7,000, my real income is $700.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.890
That's how I do my math.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:47.599
What is my bottom line number, is $700?

00:03:47.599 --> 00:03:48.849
That's the number I'm going off of.

00:03:48.849 --> 00:03:54.989
So, the second point is, to have the income
coming in from your business cover your monthly

00:03:54.989 --> 00:03:55.989
expenses.

00:03:55.989 --> 00:03:59.959
So if your monthly expenses are $2800 per
month, and your net income, you're making

00:03:59.959 --> 00:04:04.159
based on your business is three grand a month,
you're ready to go full time, because it's

00:04:04.159 --> 00:04:05.159
been covering that.

00:04:05.159 --> 00:04:09.980
Generally I like that to happen on a three
to six month period before I go full time.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:16.290
The next one before going full time as an
entrepreneur is having six months of expenses

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:17.290
covered.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.690
Now this depends on what type of a business
you have.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:22.671
If you have an investor that comes in and
they tell you.

00:04:22.671 --> 00:04:26.530
. . you know, my friend, Robert Greene who
wrote the book, 48 Laws of Power, he wanted

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:31.060
to write a book called 48 Laws of Power, and
he meets this investor in Europe and he said,

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:34.540
"Look, I'll cover your expenses for two or
three years, you go write this book."

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.240
If you have somebody that's willing to invest
for you, and cover you, then you have time.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:40.220
Then you can go full time right now and make
it happen.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:42.050
But what if you don't have an investor?

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.660
What if nobody is willing to invest in your
idea?

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:48.610
Then you have to have six months of your expenses
covered before you go full time.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:55.200
So if your expenses are $6,000 a month, you've
got $36,000, you've got six months to get

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:59.450
your business to a level where you're making
that $6,000 a month, and you've got to get

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:00.450
to work.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:03.190
Every single day counts, every single sale
counts, every single appointment counts, every

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:06.660
single call counts, every single minute counts,
because that number is you're tapping into

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:11.690
$36,000, 34, 33, 32, 31, 30, you've got to
make sure you make that money by the time

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:13.040
that 36 goes to zero.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:18.820
Point number four, on going full time, if
you're single, you have to talk to your family,

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:23.810
but very rarely, parents understand when their
kids go full time or they become entrepreneurs,

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:26.640
and they're really not supposed to unless
they've been entrepreneurs before, you've

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:33.400
got to understand that your parents, you know,
if you've been a kid for 18 years, to a parent,

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.190
you're a kid for 18 years.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:38.390
And they think you're going to be a kid forever,
right?

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:42.040
But parents believe in their kids and they
love their kids, but they don't necessarily

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:45.250
want to see them go through a failure, so
you have to go earn their respect, that you

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:46.690
can become an entrepreneur.

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:47.690
You know, there's a.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:50.570
. . my mom doesn't believe in me, and my dad
doesn't believe in me -- that happens a lot.

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:53.910
Well, you've just been a kid longer then you've
been an adult in their lives.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:56.810
You've got to go earn that respect from them
and when you do, they say, "Oh wow, we never

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:57.920
knew you could do it.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:58.920
Good job!

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.060
Now you're an entrepreneur."

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:03.751
But you've got to make sure that you have
that conversation, if you're married and you're

00:06:03.751 --> 00:06:08.630
watching this, you've got a family and kids,
you're not single, somebody single's saying,

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:09.630
"I don't care.

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:11.060
I can go full-time today," you can.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:12.060
I did.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.180
I went full time at a young age.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:16.510
Lost, failed, failed miserably, and I was
okay.

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:19.550
I was in at $49,000, I lost every single thing.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:22.560
Credit card debt, I mean, it was terrible!

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:27.020
But I didn't have kids, I didn't have responsibility,
I didn't have a wife or someone that was relying

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:28.020
on me.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:31.910
If you're married with kids, and watching
this, it is very important for you to have

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:37.030
this conversation with your partner or spouse
before going full time because you've got

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:40.292
to feed kids, family, all that stuff, if you
don't have the savings, if they know that

00:06:40.292 --> 00:06:43.790
you have the savings, if they're willing to
support you with the savings, then you can

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:44.790
go do it.

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:47.810
One of the good stories I recently saw was
from Kevin Hart.

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:50.030
Kevin Hart goes to his mom and says, "Mom,
I want to be an actor.

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:57.030
I want to be a comedian ." And his mom says,
"You're out of your mind!"

00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:59.300
He says, "Mom, please, I want to do this."

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.680
Finally, his mom says this to Kevin Hart.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:04.500
" I'll support you for one year, you don't
need to have a job.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:05.500
One year.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:10.120
But if you go and become a comedian, you better
believe, I'm working to pay your bills, for

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:14.470
one year, I will support you financially,
but you better be working hard to become a

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:15.790
professional comedian."

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:18.030
Kevin Hart today is in every other movie.

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:20.730
If you blink your eyes and open them up, he's
in another movie that he's doing.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:24.540
Kevin Hart, making millions of dollars, and
his mom's proud, but that happened, he had

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:28.980
that conversation with his family, his family
believed that he was serious, and the rest

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:30.690
is history.

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:33.280
By the way, comedians, they're entrepreneurs.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:35.560
Actors, artists, they're entrepreneurs.

00:07:35.560 --> 00:07:39.840
This is independent contract, the world where
you're going and making money on your efforts,

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:40.860
you're not getting a W-2.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.550
If you don't work, you're not making money.

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:45.700
That's the same mindset that goes into doing
what they're doing.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:49.670
The next part is timing.

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:50.670
Timing is what it is.

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:54.610
A lot of time, I have a lot of people that
I coach on going full time, and some of them

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:59.550
are afraid, so they wait way too long, and
they've been ready for a long time to go full-time.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:01.870
They just don't want to work that hard.

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:05.550
What you're really saying if you've been holding
off is that you're afraid of how much work

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:08.000
you need to put in, and you don't really want
to work that hard.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.810
That's what you're saying.

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:14.830
You know deep down inside that you can make
it, but you don't yet have the work ethic

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:17.680
and you're afraid if you really want to put
that much work in.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:20.730
The other people are the ones who do it too
early.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:24.170
And you could have waited a month or two more
months before going full time.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:27.550
There's never really a perfect timing on when
to go full time.

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:33.510
I've never seen anyone do it just perfectly,
everything perfectly on time, no matter who

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:38.629
does it it's going to be ugly at a period
of time when you decide to go from W-2 to

00:08:38.629 --> 00:08:42.479
entrepreneur full-time, but there's a timing
component.

00:08:42.479 --> 00:08:45.410
And you've gotta know if you're being way
too early or if you're being way too late.

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:48.579
Generally you'll be able to understand it
much better on when to go full time.

00:08:48.579 --> 00:08:49.579
So that's the timing part.

00:08:49.579 --> 00:08:53.499
The next one is, it takes courage, you've
got to have guts when you're going full time.

00:08:53.499 --> 00:08:54.499
You've got to have the guts.

00:08:54.499 --> 00:09:00.589
I mean, I had one of my good friends, Fred
and his wife Christie, these guys are bartenders,

00:09:00.589 --> 00:09:02.830
they've been bartending for awhile, but not
regular bartenders.

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:06.589
They're making six figures, they're doing
good and they were thinking about whether

00:09:06.589 --> 00:09:10.790
they wanted to go full time or not, and become
entrepreneurs or not, should they go become

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:14.430
this, should they go become broke, should
they do this, should they not do that, finally,

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:19.889
they did, and when they did it, his wife gets
pregnant and this is like, get married, pregnant,

00:09:19.889 --> 00:09:21.060
and start a business.

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.850
Talk about anxiety and panic on what to do.

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:28.199
But they had guts, they had courage, and they
went to work, and this month, in the month

00:09:28.199 --> 00:09:32.269
of May with their business, they're going
to net somewhere around $50,000, but if they

00:09:32.269 --> 00:09:35.740
didn't have the guts to do that, going from
six figures as bartenders, they would have

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:39.709
never made the 50, but it was never really
perfect timing for them.

00:09:39.709 --> 00:09:41.010
They just had the guts to do it.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:42.220
That's why they are where they are right now.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:51.410
The last one I'll talk to you about is similar
to what I said about talking to a loved one

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:58.199
is sitting down and letting your family know
what's going to happen with schedule and moving

00:09:58.199 --> 00:09:59.199
forward.

00:09:59.199 --> 00:10:02.320
Let me explain what I mean about schedule
and moving forward.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:06.910
You know, a lot of times, if you're married,
again, if you're married, and you've got kids

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:11.339
and you've got a family, if you don't sit
down and tell your family what to expect when

00:10:11.339 --> 00:10:16.129
you become an entrepreneur, your spouse, your
husband, your wife, your family may expect

00:10:16.129 --> 00:10:19.029
you to be coming home at 5:00, like you do
with your job.

00:10:19.029 --> 00:10:22.689
They may be expecting you to come home at
6:00, like you did at your job.

00:10:22.689 --> 00:10:25.220
That's not how it's going to be when you're
an entrepreneur.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:30.110
You need to get the buy in of your family
on the type of schedule you're going to have

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:31.321
the moment you become an entrepreneur.

00:10:31.321 --> 00:10:36.780
They need to understand that is not a 9-5,
you're going to be working double time, there

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.899
is no 9-5 as an entrepreneur.

00:10:38.899 --> 00:10:45.269
Your morning early 7:00, and you're going
to have 10:00 nights, sometimes 11:00, 12:00,

00:10:45.269 --> 00:10:49.529
but you can have Sundays with your family
and I'm a six day a week type of a guy, myself.

00:10:49.529 --> 00:10:54.029
We have a blast, we travel, we do all that
other stuff, but there needs to be that conversation

00:10:54.029 --> 00:10:59.990
taking place with family to know what to expect,
when you're going full time with business.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:04.220
Because in reality, what is the real reality
part of becoming an entrepreneur.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:05.220
Think about it.

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:06.240
So ask that question.

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:08.459
Why do you want to go become an entrepreneur?

00:11:08.459 --> 00:11:09.459
Why?

00:11:09.459 --> 00:11:10.459
Freedom?

00:11:10.459 --> 00:11:11.459
Lifestyle?

00:11:11.459 --> 00:11:12.459
Control?

00:11:12.459 --> 00:11:13.519
Building something; legacy?

00:11:13.519 --> 00:11:15.279
Being part of something very big?

00:11:15.279 --> 00:11:17.370
Solving a problem, solving a bigger problem?

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:18.910
Finding a way of doing it better?

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:20.459
Financial freedom?

00:11:20.459 --> 00:11:21.540
Victories?

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:26.779
You know, all of that comes together, but
all of that stuff is what everybody wants.

00:11:26.779 --> 00:11:32.060
You know, going through that process, like
the whole process of making a sausage, sausage

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:37.270
may taste very good, but the process is as
nasty as possible, and very few people want

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:39.040
to go through that process.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:43.499
If you do it right as an entrepreneur, and
make your transition from part-time to full

00:11:43.499 --> 00:11:47.699
time following these seven points that we've
got here, it will make for a better transition

00:11:47.699 --> 00:11:52.920
of going full time, but there's never, ever,
ever a perfect, right way of doing it.

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:57.170
No matter whoever I've seen do it, and it's
"Oh my God, you don't understand, I'm so nervous,

00:11:57.170 --> 00:11:58.899
what do I do?"

00:11:58.899 --> 00:12:03.829
As long as you know how to put your head down
and work your butt off, and know how to sell

00:12:03.829 --> 00:12:08.149
your product and figure out ways to make money
with the product that you have, and getting

00:12:08.149 --> 00:12:12.529
better, things out to pretty much work out
in your favor if you do that.

00:12:12.529 --> 00:12:16.980
Anyway, if you have any questions about going
full time, comment on the bottom and if you

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:21.300
haven't subscribed this channel, please be
sure to do so, subscribe to the channel here,

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:25.379
and if you're watching this video somewhere
else on the internet, you can always go visit

00:12:25.379 --> 00:12:28.029
PatrickBetDavid.com, for more content.

00:12:28.029 --> 00:12:29.939
Thanks for watching everybody.

00:12:29.939 --> 00:12:30.939
Take care.

00:12:30.939 --> 00:12:31.859
Bye bye.

